{"id":"_summary","shard":"Jewelry-06","checked":87,"ok":52,"issues":37,"by_kind":{"variant":25,"facets":8,"category":2,"brand":1,"icon":1},"high":5,"rule_gaps":["'pavé' derives stone=Diamond and overrides a stone actually named in the product name — 'Topas pavé' produced 3 wrong Diamond values here; a named stone must win over a setting word","the stone vocabulary misses 'Emerald', 'larvikitt', 'røkkvarts' and 'Tahitiperler', and a bare carat weight ('0,08 ct') with no 'diamant' word derives nothing","non-jewellery lands in Jewelry when 'sølv'/'Sølv' appears in the name and the breadcrumb leaf is uninformative ('Produkter', a brand path) — a Prym sewing eyelet and a silver sauce ladle both promoted this way","no row in this shard has vlabel/family: size and finish are encoded in the name only, so every hoop-size and gold/silver-finish family sits as separate top-level rows","58 of 87 rows (67%) have img=0 — David-Andersen is the dominant shop here and most of its pages queued no usable image"],"notes":"Category quality is high (85 of 87 rows are genuinely earrings and correctly in Jewelry); the real damage is variant fragmentation — 25 rows are 12 unlinked size/finish families — plus the 'pavé'→Diamond misread that puts topaz jewellery under a diamond filter."}
